---
source: crates/agentgateway/src/import/litellm.rs
description: src/tests/import/litellm/db-state-not-consumed-fields.yaml
---
source: litellm
config:
  config:
    database:
      url: "sqlite://data.db"
  gateways:
    default:
      port: 4000
  ui:
    gateways: default
  llm:
    gateways: default
    models:
      - name: chat
        provider: openAI
        params:
          model: gpt-4o
    policies:
      apiKey:
        keys:
          - keyHash: "sha256:ae058b38bff255f5aa1954d4cdd9e348b4f487293a2b6484da8d2511f581222b"
            metadata:
              name: not-consumed-key
        mode: strict
findings:
  - sourcePath: "model_list[0]"
    status: exact
    message: Imported model deployment for chat
  - sourcePath: general_settings.master_key
    status: manual
    message: "No master_key in config.yaml; if LiteLLM authenticates from the LITELLM_MASTER_KEY environment variable directly (common in Docker deployments), this importer can't see it from config.yaml alone. Set general_settings.master_key: os.environ/LITELLM_MASTER_KEY to make it visible"
  - sourcePath: "db_state.teams[team-with-limits]"
    status: manual
    message: "Team \"team-with-limits\" has its own budget_duration: \"30d\", rpm_limit: 500, tpm_limit: 1000000 that was not migrated - the budget never resets and no rate limit is applied at the team level"
  - sourcePath: "db_state.keys[0]"
    status: manual
    message: "Key has its own rpm_limit: 10, tpm_limit: 20000; agentgateway's localRateLimit has one numeric spec shared by every key behind a policy, so a per-key rate limit was not migrated. remoteRateLimit can express a per-key limit via a CEL descriptor keyed on apiKey.name, but it calls out to a separately deployed external rate-limit service for the actual counting - that service isn't something this importer can provision, so it isn't emitted automatically"
  - sourcePath: "db_state.keys[0]"
    status: unsupported
    message: "Key has a LiteLLM soft_budget ($15.00, an early-warning threshold below max_budget); agentgateway has no equivalent and only the hard max_budget was migrated"
  - sourcePath: "db_state.keys[0]"
    status: unsupported
    message: "Key is associated with LiteLLM user \"user-abc-123\"; agentgateway has no per-user construct and this association was not migrated"
  - sourcePath: "db_state.keys[0]"
    status: exact
    message: "Migrated key \"not-consumed-key\" to llm.policies.apiKey (hash-based, no plaintext)"
